  {
   "label": "Gathering",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Gathering in God’s Name"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Gathering in God’s Name"
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Greeting"
    },
    {
     "type": "versicle",
     "call": "We are gathered in the name of God, who sets us free.",
     "response": "Amen."
    },
    {
     "type": "versicle",
     "call": "The Lord be with you",
     "response": "And also with you"
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Welcome & Introduction"
    },
    {
     "type": "spacer",
     "height": 10
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Call to Worship"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Come, let us gather at the table of freedom.",
      "Divided yet longing for justice,",
      [
       "wounded yet longing for freedom.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Come, lift your voices in praise to God.",
      "Come, bring your hope and your struggle, your courage and your pain.",
      [
       "We come, for all are welcome in Christ’s presence.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "The Spirit of the Lord is upon us—",
      [
       "to lift the lowly, to break the chains.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Rise in body or in spirit, and let us worship.",
      [
       "For God is here, setting people free.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Receiving God’s Mercy",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Receiving God’s Mercy"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Receiving God’s Mercy"
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Invitation to Confession"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Friends, as we come before the God of justice and mercy,",
      "let us bring our failures and fears into the light of God’s love.",
      "Let us confess the ways we have not acted justly,",
      "and open ourselves to God’s transforming grace."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Confession"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "Loving God,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "we admit that we have done wrong:",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "in our thoughts, words, and actions.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "Please forgive us.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Help us to change,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and guide us in the future.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "Help us to live justly,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "to show mercy,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and to walk humbly with you.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Absolution"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "God, the source of all mercy and renewal,",
      "forgives you and sets you free;",
      "restoring you in the likeness of God,",
      "that your life may reflect love and goodness,",
      "to the praise of the Holy One, now and always.",
      [
       "Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Giving Praise",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Gathering in God’s Name"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Giving Praise"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "We give thanks to you, gracious God,",
      [
       "for your mercy restores and your grace makes us whole.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "22px 0 24px"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "You have drawn near in every age—",
      [
       "freeing the captives, forgiving the broken, feeding the hungry.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "From the beginning you made the world in goodness,",
      [
       "a gift of grace where salvation is written in every living thing.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "In Jesus, your Word became flesh,",
      [
       "bringing salvation to the world and grace upon grace.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "By your Spirit, you breathe life into our weary souls",
      [
       "and set us again on the path of joy.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "We give you thanks and praise,",
      [
       "now and always. Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Prayer of the Day",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Bible and Teaching"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Prayer of the Day"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "God of the long night,",
      "you do not want our noise and our festivals",
      "but justice rolling down like waters.",
      "Keep our lamps trimmed with the oil of right living,",
      "so that when the cry goes up at midnight",
      "we may be ready to go out and meet you;",
      "through Jesus Christ our Lord.",
      [
       "Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "22px 0 0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Amos 5",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Bible and Teaching"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Readings"
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "Readings are from the Common English Bible.",
     "margin": "16px 0 0"
    },
    {
     "type": "worktitle",
     "text": "Amos 5:18–24",
     "sub": "First reading",
     "margin": "30px 0 18px"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "A reading from the prophet Amos."
     ],
     "margin": "0 0 20px"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Doom to those who desire the day of the Lord!",
      "Why do you want the day of the Lord?",
      "It is darkness, not light;",
      "as if someone fled from a lion,",
      "and was met by a bear;",
      "or sought refuge in a house,",
      "rested a hand against the wall,",
      "and was bitten by a snake."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Isn’t the day of the Lord darkness, not light;",
      "all dark with no brightness in it?",
      "I hate, I reject your festivals;",
      "I don’t enjoy your joyous assemblies."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "If you bring me your entirely burned offerings and gifts of food—",
      "I won’t be pleased;",
      "I won’t even look at your offerings of well-fed animals."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Take away the noise of your songs;",
      "I won’t listen to the melody of your harps."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "But let justice roll down like waters,",
      "and righteousness like an ever-flowing stream."
     ],
     "margin": "0 0 22px"
    },
    {
     "type": "versicle",
     "call": "This is the word of the Lord",
     "response": "Thanks be to God",
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Gospel",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Bible and Teaching"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Gospel"
    },
    {
     "type": "worktitle",
     "text": "Matthew 25:1–13",
     "margin": "22px 0 18px"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      {
       "segments": [
        [
         "Alleluia! ",
         ""
        ],
        [
         "Alleluia!",
         "all"
        ]
       ]
      },
      {
       "segments": [
        [
         "Keep alert, because you don’t know the day or the hour, says the Lord. ",
         ""
        ],
        [
         "Alleluia!",
         "all"
        ]
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "versicle",
     "call": "The Lord be with you",
     "response": "And also with you"
    },
    {
     "type": "versicle",
     "call": "A reading from the Good News according to Matthew.",
     "response": "Glory to you Lord Jesus Christ"
    },
    {
     "type": "prose",
     "margin": "0 0 22px",
     "paragraphs": [
      "“At that time the kingdom of heaven will be like ten young bridesmaids who took their lamps and went out to meet the groom. Now five of them were wise, and the other five were foolish. The foolish ones took their lamps but didn’t bring oil for them. But the wise ones took their lamps and also brought containers of oil.",
      "“When the groom was late in coming, they all became drowsy and went to sleep. But at midnight there was a cry, ‘Look, the groom! Come out to meet him.’",
      "“Then all those bridesmaids got up and prepared their lamps. But the foolish bridesmaids said to the wise ones, ‘Give us some of your oil, because our lamps have gone out.’",
      "“But the wise bridesmaids replied, ‘No, because if we share with you, there won’t be enough for our lamps and yours. We have a better idea. You go to those who sell oil and buy some for yourselves.’ But while they were gone to buy oil, the groom came. Those who were ready went with him into the wedding. Then the door was shut.",
      "“Later the other bridesmaids came and said, ‘Lord, lord, open the door for us.’",
      "“But he replied, ‘I tell you the truth, I don’t know you.’",
      "“Therefore, keep alert, because you don’t know the day or the hour."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "versicle",
     "call": "This is the good news of the Lord",
     "response": "Praise to you Lord Jesus Christ",
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Sermon & Affirmation",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Bible and Teaching"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Sermon"
    },
    {
     "type": "spacer"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Affirmation"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "We believe in God,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "whose love is unending,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "whose mercy restores,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and whose promise holds creation fast.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "22px 0 24px"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "We believe in Christ,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Word made flesh,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "friend of the outcast,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "light in the darkness, risen and true.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "We believe the Spirit moves among us,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "stirring courage,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "kindling compassion,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and weaving us into one.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "We believe the Church is a living body,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "open to all,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "rooted in grace,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "sent to serve in love.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "This is our faith,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "our calling,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "our song of praise.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Prayers & Peace",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Prayers and Peace"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Prayers of the People"
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Intercessions"
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "Led by the intercessor. Everyone responds to each petition with:"
    },
    {
     "type": "versicle",
     "call": "Lord in your mercy",
     "response": "Hear our prayer"
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Prayer for St Aidan’s"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "God of Mission,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "you call us to share your love.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Send your Holy Spirit to guide us",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "in deepening our discipleship,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "in welcoming everyone,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and in sharing your love with courage.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "Help St Aidan’s grow",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "in faith, diversity,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and service to our community.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Conclusion to Prayers"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Loving God, you hear our prayers.",
      [
       "By your Spirit,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "guide us to live with open hearts,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "trusting in your presence",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and grace,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "through Jesus Christ our Lord. Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "spacer"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Greeting of Peace"
    },
    {
     "type": "versicle",
     "call": "We are the body of Christ",
     "response": "His Spirit is with us",
     "margin": "22px 0 24px"
    },
    {
     "type": "versicle",
     "call": "The peace of the Lord be with you",
     "response": "And also with you",
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Offertory Hymn (1–2)",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Offertory Hymn"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "I Want to Walk as a Child of the Light"
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "TIS 643 · verses 1–2",
     "margin": "16px 0 22px"
    },
    {
     "type": "hymn",
     "verses": [
      [
       "I want to walk as a child of the light.",
       "I want to follow Jesus.",
       "God set the stars to give light to the world.",
       "The star of my life is Jesus."
      ],
      [
       "In him there is no darkness at all;",
       "the night and the day are both alike.",
       "The Lamb is the light of the city of God;",
       "shine in my heart, Lord Jesus."
      ],
      [
       "I want to see the brightness of God,",
       "I want to look at Jesus,",
       "clear sun of righteousness, shine on my path,",
       "and show me the way to the Father."
      ],
      [
       "In him there is no darkness at all;",
       "the night and the day are both alike.",
       "The Lamb is the light of the city of God;",
       "shine in my heart, Lord Jesus."
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "note",
     "text": "CCLI Licence #309884"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Offertory Hymn (3)",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Offertory Hymn"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "I Want to Walk as a Child of the Light"
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "TIS 643 · verse 3",
     "margin": "16px 0 22px"
    },
    {
     "type": "hymn",
     "verses": [
      [
       "I’m looking for the coming of Christ,",
       "I want to be with Jesus.",
       "When we have run with patience the race,",
       "we shall know the joy of Jesus."
      ],
      [
       "In him there is no darkness at all;",
       "the night and the day are both alike.",
       "The Lamb is the light of the city of God;",
       "shine in my heart, Lord Jesus."
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "note",
     "text": "CCLI Licence #309884"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Introduction to Communion",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Holy Communion"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Introduction to Communion"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Here we gather now at Christ’s table—",
      "a table of justice, liberation, and grace."
     ],
     "margin": "22px 0 20px"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Here we remember the story of Jesus",
      "who fed the hungry,",
      "welcomed the marginalised,",
      "and proclaimed good news to the poor."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "At this table everyone is welcome.",
      "Come as you are."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "spacer"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "The Thanksgiving Prayer"
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Sursum Corda"
    },
    {
     "type": "versicle",
     "call": "The Lord be with you.",
     "response": "And also with you"
    },
    {
     "type": "versicle",
     "call": "Lift up your hearts.",
     "response": "We lift them to the Lord."
    },
    {
     "type": "versicle",
     "call": "Let us give thanks to the Lord our God.",
     "response": "It is right to give our thanks and praise.",
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Preface",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "The Thanksgiving Prayer"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Preface"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "It is right to give you thanks,",
      "God of justice and mercy."
     ],
     "margin": "22px 0 24px"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "You created the world in love,",
      "giving us land, water, people, and purpose.",
      [
       "You called us to live in freedom and community.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "You never gave up on us.",
      "You sent prophets to challenge injustice",
      "and show us a better way.",
      "In Jesus, you came among us—",
      [
       "healing, teaching,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and walking the path of justice.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "You created us in love",
      [
       "and called us to live in freedom.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "So with all who hunger for freedom,",
      "we give you thanks and praise,",
      "saying together:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "Blessed is our God,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "who brings down the mighty",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and lifts up the lowly.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Blessed is our God, forever.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Words of Institution",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "The Thanksgiving Prayer"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Words of Institution"
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Bread"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "On the night of his giving,",
      "Jesus blessed and broke the bread.",
      "He shared it with his friends, saying:",
      "Take and eat.",
      "This is my body, broken for you.",
      "As you do this, you are remembering me.",
      [
       "Lord my God.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Wine"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "After they had eaten,",
      "he took the cup of wine,",
      "gave thanks, and said:",
      "Drink this, all of you.",
      "This is my blood of the new covenant,",
      "poured out for you and for all,",
      "to reconcile and to heal.",
      "As you do this, you are remembering me.",
      [
       "Lord my God.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Acclamation to Doxology",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "The Thanksgiving Prayer"
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Acclamation"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Let us proclaim the mystery of faith.",
      [
       "Christ has died to set us free.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Christ is risen to make us whole.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Christ will come again with justice and joy.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Epiclesis"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Come, Holy Spirit,",
      "rest upon these gifts of bread and wine,",
      "that they may be for us the life of Christ.",
      [
       "As we share this meal,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "make us one with each other,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and one in Christ, our risen Lord.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Doxology"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Gathered with angels and archangels,",
      "and with every generation who has trusted your love,",
      "we join the hymn of heaven:",
      [
       "Holy, holy, holy Lord,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "God of power and might,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "heaven and earth are full of your glory.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Praise to you in the highest.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Lord’s Prayer to Invitation",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Holy Communion"
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "The Lord’s Prayer"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "Father, uphold the holiness of your name.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Bring in your kingdom.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Give us the bread we need for today.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Forgive us our sins,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "for we also forgive everyone who has wronged us.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "And save us in times of trial.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "For you are worthy,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "our Lord and God,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "to receive glory and honour and power,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "because you created all things.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Breaking the Bread"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "We break and share this bread,",
      "a sign of Christ’s life poured out for us.",
      [
       "Though we are many, we are made one,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "for we all eat of the one bread.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Invitation to Communion"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "The gifts of God for the people of God.",
      [
       "Graciously nourish us, O Christ,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "so that we who try to follow you",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "may receive food for the journey",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and be bound in solidarity",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "with all who walk in your way.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Communion Anthem",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Communion Anthem"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Jesus Christ, Be the Wine of Grace"
    },
    {
     "type": "spacer",
     "height": 12
    },
    {
     "type": "hymn",
     "verses": [
      [
       "In the singing, in the silence,",
       "in the hands expectant, open,",
       "in the blessing, in the breaking,",
       "in the presence at this table"
      ],
      [
       "Jesus Christ, Jesus Christ,",
       "be the wine of grace.",
       "Jesus Christ, Jesus Christ,",
       "be the bread of peace."
      ],
      [
       "In the question, in the answer,",
       "in the moment of acceptance,",
       "in the heart’s cry, in the healing,",
       "in the circle of your people."
      ],
      [
       "Jesus Christ, Jesus Christ,",
       "be the wine of grace.",
       "Jesus Christ, Jesus Christ,",
       "be the bread of peace."
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "note",
     "text": "CCLI Licence #309884"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Receiving Communion",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Receiving Communion"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "What Does the Lord Require of You"
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "TIS 751",
     "margin": "16px 0 22px"
    },
    {
     "type": "hymn",
     "verses": [
      [
       "What does the Lord require of you?",
       "What does the Lord require of you?",
       "Justice, kindness,",
       "walk humbly with your God.",
       "To seek justice, and love kindness,",
       "and walk humbly with your God."
      ],
      [
       "What does the Lord require of you?",
       "What does the Lord require of you?",
       "Justice, kindness,",
       "walk humbly with your God.",
       "To seek justice, and love kindness,",
       "and walk humbly with your God."
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "note",
     "text": "CCLI Licence #309884"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Sending Out",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Sending Out God’s People"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Prayer after Communion"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "God our liberator,",
      "we thank you for feeding us at your table.",
      "Let this holy meal strengthen us",
      "to act with justice and love.",
      "Send us out to be your hands in the world."
     ],
     "margin": "22px 0 24px"
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Gratitude for Communion"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "Lord,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "we have broken your bread",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and received your life.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "By the power of your Spirit",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "keep us always in your love",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "through Jesus Christ our Lord.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "spacer"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Notices"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Blessing & Dismissal",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Sending Out God’s People"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Blessing"
    },
    {
     "type": "versicle",
     "call": "The Lord be with you",
     "response": "And also with you",
     "margin": "22px 0 24px"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "May the God who breaks every chain",
      "and sets the captives free,",
      "bless you with courage, vision, and hope."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "And the blessing of God,",
      "Creator, Liberator, and Sustainer,",
      "be with you always.",
      [
       "Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "spacer"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Dismissal"
    },
    {
     "type": "versicle",
     "call": "Go in peace, to love and serve the Lord",
     "response": "In the name of Christ. Amen.",
     "margin": "22px 0 0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Sending Hymn (1–2)",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Sending Hymn"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "At the Name of Jesus"
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "TIS 231 · verses 1–2",
     "margin": "16px 0 22px"
    },
    {
     "type": "hymn",
     "verses": [
      [
       "At the name of Jesus",
       "every knee shall bow,",
       "every tongue confess him",
       "King of glory now.",
       "This the Father’s pleasure,",
       "that we call him Lord,",
       "who from the beginning",
       "was the mighty Word."
      ],
      [
       "Humbled for a season,",
       "to receive a name",
       "from the lips of sinners",
       "unto whom he came,",
       "faithfully he bore it",
       "spotless to the last,",
       "brought it back victorious",
       "when from death he passed."
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "note",
     "text": "CCLI Licence #309884"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Sending Hymn (3–4)",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Sending Hymn"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "At the Name of Jesus"
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "TIS 231 · verses 3–4",
     "margin": "16px 0 22px"
    },
    {
     "type": "hymn",
     "verses": [
      [
       "In your hearts enthrone him;",
       "there let him make new",
       "all that is not holy,",
       "all that is not true.",
       "He is God the Saviour,",
       "he is Christ the Lord,",
       "ever to be worshipped,",
       "trusted and adored."
      ],
      [
       "When this same Lord Jesus",
       "shall appear again",
       "in his Father’s glory,",
       "there with him to reign,",
       "then may we adore him,",
       "all before him bow,",
       "as our hearts confess him",
       "King of glory now."
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "note",
     "text": "CCLI Licence #309884"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}